│ What will change (11)                                                                                              │
│  1 Verify the Tor Project signing key (A3C4F0F979CAA22CDBA8F512EE8CBC9E886DDD89) and install                       │
│    /usr/share/keyrings/deb.torproject.org-keyring.gpg                                                              │
│  2 Write /etc/apt/sources.list.d/tor.sources for bookworm                                                          │
│  3 Install packages in one apt transaction: tor deb.torproject.org-keyring nyx unattended-upgrades apt-listchanges │
│  4 Create tor instance relay2 with tor-instance-create relay2 if it does not exist (user _tor-relay2,              │
│    /etc/tor/instances/relay2/torrc, DataDirectory /var/lib/tor-instances/relay2, unit tor@relay2)                  │
│  5 Write /etc/sysctl.d/60-tor-relay.conf (ephemeral ports 15000-64000; nf_conntrack_max 262144 if conntrack is     │
│    loaded) and apply it with sysctl                                                                                │
│  6 Raise LimitNOFILE to 65536 with /etc/systemd/system/tor@.service.d/60-tor-relay-setup.conf, only if             │
│    tor@.service allows fewer open files                                                                            │
│  7 Write /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52tor-relay-unattended-upgrades (security updates + Tor Project packages)             │
│  8 Write /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/20auto-upgrades                                                                       │
│  9 Back up and replace /etc/tor/instances/relay2/torrc after tor --verify-config accepts the new version           │
│ 10 ufw allow 9002/tcp comment 'Tor relay ORPort'                                                                   │
│ 11 Enable and restart tor@relay2                                                                                   │
